                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Its laughable that there was a \"QA Team\" for this game. There are bugs just about every in game day. Certain things will not spawn on the first day of launching the game, but work afterwards. There's a random bush in the middle of town that can't decide what color it is. Sometimes flowers don't spawn when they should, making you waste one of your two trips for the day. The developer also didn't add any contextual dialog based on where you are with the story. Someone who you shouldn't be seeing is just hanging out, despite the story's current progress. \r\n\r\nThere are some quality of life things that I found surprising were not in the game. You cannot use the D Pad AT ALL. You have to navigate your inventory with the joystick, which my partner and I found annoying. You can't close ANY menus with the B button as any sane person would try to do. You have to navigate down to the \"Close\" button to close most menus. In fact, I don't think the B button is even used in the game. Reopening your inventory doesn't remember where you were so you have to navigate to the item you're working with every time you're interacting with it. There's also no \"sort\" option for the inventory. Sure you can filter it, but its still a cluttered mess.\r\n\r\nThe game also runs terribly. I can't believe walking into a building would take more 8 seconds to load at times. The loading screen will almost always stutter trying to load and scene changes.\r\n\r\nI could go on... Would I recommend this game? No, certainly not for the $20 I paid. It feels as if this was rushed out to meet a deadline and the dev team never bothered to fix any bugs. Any of these would have been discovered if anyone on their team had played the game. Which leads me to believe this game was released and the dev team dropped it. My partner and I will probably finish trying to max out the relationships with the villagers, but I don't foresee us picking up this game again. Save yourself $20 and play something else.",
